---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../../../components/Icon.astro';
import Workflow from '../../../components/Workflow.astro';
import { flows } from '../../../data/flows';
---

<Layout
  title="Web3, crypto & wallet development"
  description="Soft Task develops Web3 applications, crypto and token platforms, wallets and smart-contract integrations. Explore product scope, governance and delivery considerations."
>
  <section class="web3-product-cover wrap">
    <div class="breadcrumb">
      <a href="/services/blockchain-engineering/">Blockchain & Web3</a>
      <span>/ Web3 development</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h1>
        Build for the people
        <br />
        behind the wallet.
      </h1>
      <p>
        Web3 and crypto development connects a usable product with contracts, transaction behaviour
        and a clearly defined operating model.
      </p>
    </div>
    <nav aria-label="Web3 development topics">
      <a href="#applications">Applications</a>
      <a href="#tokens">Crypto & tokens</a>
      <a href="#wallets">Wallets</a>
      <a href="#contracts">Smart contracts</a>
    </nav>
  </section>
  <section class="web3-product-grid wrap">
    <article id="applications">
      <span>Product experience</span>
      <h2>Decentralised applications</h2>
      <p>
        Develop the interface and services around a decentralised workflow. Account connection,
        transaction signing, network selection and confirmation states need to be understandable to
        the user.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Web3 application interfaces and backend integrations</li>
        <li>Marketplace and token-enabled workflows</li>
        <li>On-chain event indexing and application data</li>
        <li>Transaction status, fees and exception handling</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
    <article id="tokens">
      <span>Asset lifecycle</span>
      <h2>Crypto & token development</h2>
      <p>
        Define the purpose, rules and controls of a token before implementation. Token contracts,
        allocation mechanisms and administrative functions should reflect the agreed product and
        governance model.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Token and crypto platform architecture</li>
        <li>Issuance, transfer and lifecycle logic</li>
        <li>Administrative permissions and governance</li>
        <li>Integration with wallets and business systems</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
    <article id="wallets">
      <span>Control & ownership</span>
      <h2>Wallet development</h2>
      <p>
        Wallet design begins with who controls the keys. A custodial model and a user-controlled
        model have different operating responsibilities, recovery paths and integration
        requirements.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Wallet interfaces and account connection</li>
        <li>Signing and transaction submission flows</li>
        <li>Balance views and transaction history</li>
        <li>Integration with the selected custody architecture</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
    <article id="contracts">
      <span>Rules & execution</span>
      <h2>Smart-contract engineering</h2>
      <p>
        Specify what a contract should do, who may change it and how failures are handled. Testing
        must cover the relationship between contract behaviour and the application that depends on
        it.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Contract specifications and implementation</li>
        <li>Unit, integration and scenario testing</li>
        <li>Deployment and upgrade procedures</li>
        <li>Independent review coordination where commissioned</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap section">
    <Workflow
      id="web3-development"
      title="Connect the user journey to the ledger"
      steps={flows.web3}
    />
  </section>
  <section class="web3-ownership">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>
        The operating model
        <br />
        is part of the product.
      </h2>
      <div>
        <p>
          Define signing authority, permissions, network dependencies, transaction monitoring and
          reconciliation. Identify who can pause an operation, approve a change and investigate an
          exception.
        </p>
        <p>
          Engineering does not establish permission to operate a financial service. Applicable
          market requirements, independent reviews and operating responsibilities must be addressed
          in the project scope with the appropriate specialists.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="product-next wrap">
    <div>
      <h2>Building an exchange?</h2>
      <p>
        Explore the application, execution, wallet and reconciliation work behind centralised and
        decentralised exchange platforms.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/services/blockchain-engineering/exchange-development/">
        Exchange development <Icon />
      </a>
    </div>
    <a class="button" href="/contact/?service=blockchain-engineering">
      Discuss a Web3 project <Icon />
    </a>
  </section>
</Layout>
